Use the given fact schema. Instead of copying source text, a value may be {"$source":"L12"}
or {"$source":["L12","L13"]}. These copy EXACT whole source lines. Pick original body lines
only for body; keep draft/preview/routing indicators in your classification decision.
For a structured table you selected, replace an array with {"$rows":"T0",
"header":[<EXACT header cells>],"fields":{"material_number":{"$cell":0},"quantity":{"$cell":1}}}.
Cell numbers start at zero. Raw numbers may use {"$cell":1,"locale":"de-DE"} only when
that locale is explicitly evidenced. A scalar may use {"$line":"EXACT label including colon:"}
if exactly one source line starts with it; its suffix is copied. Never use a line label
whose value needs interpretation. Set reuse true ONLY if the layout alone supplies ALL
values through cells/labelled lines. Interpreted dates, status meanings, booleans, defaults,
IDs and commercial semantics must stay ordinary values and reuse false. Source line
pointers also require reuse false. On ambiguity use ordinary schema values, omit
unshown fields, and reuse false. Source URLs remain attached by the caller.
"""

